    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d449">

                <pb facs="0449" n="437" sameAs="frus:frus1939v01/pg437"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/383: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Rumania</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gunther</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bucharest</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-09-18T13:00:00+03:00">September 18,
                            1939—1 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 7:35 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>212. Gafencu<anchor n="62" xml:id="d449-f1"/> received yesterday assurances from
                    Molotov that the Russian advance into Poland should not be considered menacing
                    to Rumania. One does not know however how little faith to place in these
                    assurances. It all depends upon what deal has already been made between Russia
                    and Germany.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gunther</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d449-f1" n="62" xml:id="d449-f1-content">
                <p>Grigore Gafencu, Rumanian Minister for Foreign Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
